///$tab 00 Main
/*=====================================================================================
  APPLICATION : Rental Analytics - Enterprise Reference Model
  PURPOSE     : Production-shaped Qlik Sense application used as a migration baseline.
  SOURCE      : PostgreSQL "pagila" (Aiven) - schemas public + mig
  ARCHITECTURE: Direct extract from Postgres -> transform in memory -> star schema

  PORTABILITY TO SUPERSET
    Everything this app displays comes from a table or view in Postgres. There is no
    generated data, no QVD layer, no sampling filter and no scaling expression in this
    script. Point Superset at the same objects and it returns identical rows with no
    additional configuration.

      mig.v_synthetic_sales   129,043 rows   the volume extension, pre-sampled
      mig.v_budget              2,336 rows   plan, pre-scaled to match the sample
      mig.fx_rates              7,671 rows   EUR / GBP / KZT daily
      public.payment           16,049 rows   real ERP transactions, never sampled
      public.film, actor, film_actor, film_category, category, language,
             address, city, country, customer, staff, store, inventory, rental

    The subset is defined ONCE, in the database, by mig.v_sample_config. To change
    density, edit subset-views.sql and re-run it. Nothing here or in Superset changes.

  RELOAD PERFORMANCE - roughly 42 seconds
    The connection matters more than the row count. The original used
    UseDeclareFetch=1;Fetch=200 - 200 rows per network round trip, ~2,580 trips for
    516k rows, measured at 300s. PostgreSQL_pagila_bulk uses
    UseDeclareFetch=0;Fetch=20000 and did the same 516k rows in 78s. Read-only.

  DETERMINISM
    Rand() appears nowhere. mig.synthetic_sales was built from md5 hashes of stable
    seeds, so reloads are byte-identical. The only derived values in this script are
    two documented modulo expressions on DimFilm and DimCustomer, each of which keeps
    its raw source value alongside.

  DO NOT load ad-hoc spreadsheets into this app. A Sheet1$ table carrying Country and
  Date columns was added on 28/08 and closed a circular reference, forcing Qlik to mark
  FactSales as a LOOSE table. Selections then stop propagating. Removed 28/08.
=====================================================================================*/

SET ThousandSep=',';
SET DecimalSep='.';
SET MoneyThousandSep=',';
SET MoneyDecimalSep='.';
SET MoneyFormat='$#,##0.00;-$#,##0.00';
SET TimeFormat='hh:mm:ss';
SET DateFormat='DD/MM/YYYY';
SET TimestampFormat='DD/MM/YYYY hh:mm:ss[.fff]';
SET FirstWeekDay=0;
SET BrokenWeeks=0;
SET ReferenceDay=4;
SET FirstMonthOfYear=1;
SET CollationLocale='en-US';
SET MonthNames='Jan;Feb;Mar;Apr;May;Jun;Jul;Aug;Sep;Oct;Nov;Dec';
SET LongMonthNames='January;February;March;April;May;June;July;August;September;October;November;December';
SET DayNames='Mon;Tue;Wed;Thu;Fri;Sat;Sun';
SET LongDayNames='Monday;Tuesday;Wednesday;Thursday;Friday;Saturday;Sunday';
SET NumericalAbbreviation='3:k;6:M;9:G;12:T;15:P;18:E;21:Z;24:Y;-3:m;-6:µ;-9:n;-12:p;-15:f;-18:a;-21:z;-24:y';

SET ErrorMode=1;
SET HidePrefix='%';